NCBI code: public-domain government work; see LICENSE. Third-party code retains
its own notices, collected by scripts/toolchains/add_blast.py into the payload.
Citation: Camacho C et al. BMC Bioinformatics 2009;10:421.
doi:10.1186/1471-2105-10-421
Bundled for Linux x86_64 (source build with glibc 2.17), macOS Intel/Apple
Silicon (source builds targeting macOS 12.3), and Windows x86_64 (official
NCBI archive). Archive SHA-256 values are pinned in add_blast.py and
blast_prebuilt.py and recorded in the payload's blast-smoke.json.
HICT_BLASTN_BIN remains an optional override.
macOS source builds backport zlib's classic-Mac-OS platform guard from
https://github.com/madler/zlib/blob/v1.3.1/zutil.h to the bundled zlib 1.2.12.
The altered guard is marked in the source. Original notices are retained;
blast-source-patches.json records the header hashes and upstream reference.
macOS source builds also repair the bundled BitMagic bulk-insert iterator's
copy/move assignment calls to removed temporary-block methods, using the same
block allocator API as its constructors and destructor. This local fix is
marked in bm.h; all original copyright/license notices remain intact.
Related upstream report: https://github.com/ncbi/ncbi-cxx-toolkit-public/issues/20
blast-source-patches.json contains a patches array with both header records.
Windows nghttp2.dll is upstream nghttp2 1.40.0, MIT; see nghttp2-COPYING.
https://github.com/nghttp2/nghttp2/blob/v1.40.0/COPYING
Windows app-local VC runtime: see Microsoft-Visual-Cpp-NOTICE.txt.
